Cache fs.existsSync calls in plugin scan path
TL;DR
Plugin manifest discovery and bundled directory scanning call fs.existsSync 41 times across hot paths during cold start. These are synchronous calls in the main event loop. CPU profiling on Windows shows fs.existsSync self-time of 25.4 seconds during a single cold start.
This PR adds a process-level memoization cache for those calls. After the patch, existsSync self-time drops to 1.3 seconds — a 95% reduction.
Motivation
While debugging slow cold starts (openclaw agent --local taking 48+ seconds before any agent work begins), I captured a CPU profile via node --cpu-prof. The Sandwich view in speedscope showed fs.existsSync as the single largest self-time contributor.
Before:
