The remaining ~1.3 s of fs.existsSync self-time comes from call sites elsewhere (e.g. control-ui-assets.ts and other files with low call counts) that are not part of this PR.
The patch was also applied to a 4.29 production install (manually patching dist/bundle-manifest-*.js) and verified by:

openclaw --version returns normally (no stack overflow / no recursion bug)
openclaw gateway --force brings the gateway up cleanly to [gateway] ready
All plugins load (acpx, bonjour, browser, device-pair, feishu, file-transfer, memory-core, openclaw-weixin, phone-control, talk-voice)

What this PR does NOT fix
The original investigation was triggered by a 200–300 s cold-start complaint. After this PR, most of the wall-clock cold-start time remains — it's dominated by other stages visible in the embedded-run trace summary, e.g.:
runtime-plugins:    54s
core-plugin-tools:  97s
system-prompt:      73s
stream-setup:       51s
These look architectural (likely candidates for #67000 — warm reuse / session standby) and are out of scope for this PR.
Risk
Low. The cache only memoizes return values of a pure read-only filesystem query, scoped to the lifetime of a single Node process. The path set being checked is stable during plugin discovery (no scan-time path creation). If a future caller needs invalidation, invalidateExistsSyncCache is available.
Notes for reviewers

All three modified files import the new existsSyncCached from ../shared/cached-fs.js (or the appropriate relative path).
The native fs.existsSync in cached-fs.ts is the only direct call to the Node API — this is intentional and correct (the cache function itself uses fs.existsSync to populate the cache; the recursion-via-replacement bug was caught and fixed during development).
No existing tests were modified. Adding a cached-fs.test.ts would be a reasonable follow-up.
